{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And he called there on the name of YHWH, the Everlasting El</b> — the meaning of the verse is that he called upon the name of YHWH who governs through His power over time. Or, that 'heaven and earth' may be called 'עולם' (everlasting), in the language that constantly appears in the words of our Sages. And by this he made known that Abraham called out and made known to all creatures the secret of the governance of the world in its totality — that it is through the name of YHWH, who endures in power, who has mastery over all. And the Rav said in Moreh HaNevukhim (II:13) that this alludes to the eternity of El, for he made known that He exists prior to time. But Onkelos (Targum Onkelos on Genesis 21:33) said regarding 'וַיִּקְרָא' ('and he called') that it is prayer:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The phrase הֶחָסִין בַּכֹּחַ (literally 'the one who is stored / contained in power') is rendered as 'endures in power'; the expression is unusual and may carry a technical philosophical or kabbalistic sense left deliberately literal here."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:32:55.955848567Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}